Do not block on the boot control HAL to name the super partition.

GetSuperPartition() asks android.hardware.boot.IBootControl for the current
slot so it can build fs_mgr_get_super_partition_name(slot).
BootControlClient::WaitForService() first checks AServiceManager_isDeclared()
and then calls AServiceManager_waitForService(), which never returns while a
declared instance is missing.

A device tree that ships a recovery VINTF fragment for
android.hardware.boot (needed by update_engine_sideload) therefore declares
the instance from early boot, while the vendor HAL binary itself lives on
/vendor - a logical partition TWRP only maps and mounts later in
ProcessFstab(), i.e. after this call.  The result is a deadlock: recovery
stops at

  gui2: 1272x2800, ... scale 1.06
  => Linking mtab
  => Processing /etc/recovery.fstab

with the main thread parked in binder waitForService, no /dev/block/mapper
devices and fstab.additional still unset (so the HAL never starts either).

Let the device tree pin the name with ro.twrp.super_partition and skip the
HAL lookup entirely.  The remaining WaitForService() call sites
(SetActiveSlot, Flash_Current_Twrp, update_verifier) run from user actions
long after /vendor is available, so they keep using the real HAL.

diff --git a/partitionmanager.cpp b/partitionmanager.cpp
index 26c9e2d..2ca44f1 100755
--- a/partitionmanager.cpp
+++ b/partitionmanager.cpp
@@ -3484,6 +3484,17 @@ bool TWPartitionManager::PrepareAllSuperVolumes() {
 }
 
 std::string TWPartitionManager::GetSuperPartition() {
+  // A device tree may pin the name: on this platform super is a plain partition,
+  // while the boot control HAL that would report the slot lives on /vendor, which
+  // TWRP only mounts later in ProcessFstab().  A recovery VINTF fragment that
+  // declares android.hardware.boot makes BootControlClient::WaitForService()
+  // block until the instance registers, so asking for it here deadlocks the
+  // startup ("=> Processing /etc/recovery.fstab" being the last log line).
+  const std::string pinned_super = android::base::GetProperty("ro.twrp.super_partition", "");
+  if (!pinned_super.empty()) {
+    LOGINFO("Using pinned super partition '%s'\n", pinned_super.c_str());
+    return GetByNamePath(pinned_super);
+  }
   std::string super_device = "super";
 #ifdef AB_OTA_UPDATER
